"kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltextdirection","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLTextDirection","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTextDirection","abstract":[{"text":"The text-direction type is used to adjust and override the Unicode bidirectional text algorithm, similar to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the Directionality data category in the W3C Internationalization Tag Set recommendation. Values are ltr (left-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to-right embed), rtl (right-to-left embed), lro (left-to-right bidi-override), and rlo (right-to-left bidi-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"override). The default value is ltr. This type is typically used by applications that store text in left-to-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"right visual order rather than logical order. Such applications can use the lro value to better communicate","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with other applications that more fully support bidirectional text.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"}}}